  "text": "URL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ravikumar9199_interviewexperience-amazon-backendengineering-activity-7419793472636866560-qZ7e\nContent-Type: text/html\nMethod: raw\n\n---\n\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n\n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n\n    \n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <head>\n        <meta name=\"pageKey\" content=\"d_public_post\">\n          \n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"max-image-preview:large, noarchive\">\n    <meta name=\"bingbot\" content=\"max-image-preview:large, archive\">\n  \n<!----><!---->        <meta name=\"locale\" content=\"en_US\">\n<!---->        <meta id=\"config\" data-app-version=\"1.2.2092\" data-call-tree-id=\"AAZbdVJcug93rpahZbETNw==\" data-multiproduct-name=\"feedcontent-guest-frontend\" data-service-name=\"feedcontent-guest-frontend\" data-browser-id=\"50f82d06-014d-4f2b-85d1-c993d16299c8\" data-is-bot=\"true\" data-enable-page-view-heartbeat-tracking data-page-instance=\"urn:li:page:d_public_post;YIONrONyR5WWy1ZJc0HH5g==\" data-disable-jsbeacon-pagekey-suffix=\"false\" data-member-id=\"0\" data-should-use-full-url-in-pve-path=\"true\" data-dna-member-lix-treatment=\"enabled\" data-human-member-lix-treatment=\"enabled\" data-dfp-member-lix-treatment=\"control\" data-sync-apfc-headers-lix-treatment=\"control\" data-sync-apfc-cb-lix-treatment=\"control\" data-recaptcha-v3-integration-lix-value=\"control\" data-network-interceptor-lix-value=\"control\" data-is-epd-audit-event-enabled=\"false\" data-is-feed-sponsored-tracking-kill-switch-enabled=\"false\" data-sequence-auto-redirect-before-request-enabled=\"true\">\n\n        <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ravikumar9199_interviewexperience-amazon-backendengineering-activity-7419793472636866560-qZ7e\">\n<!----><!---->\n<!---->\n<!---->\n          <meta property=\"al:android:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ravikumar9199_interviewexperience-amazon-backendengineering-activity-7419793472636866560-qZ7e\">\n          <meta property=\"al:android:package\" content=\"com.linkedin.android\">\n          <meta property=\"al:android:app_name\" content=\"LinkedIn\">\n          <meta property=\"al:ios:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ravikumar9199_interviewexperience-amazon-backendengineering-activity-7419793472636866560-qZ7e\">\n          <meta property=\"al:ios:app_store_id\" content=\"288429040\">\n          <meta property=\"al:ios:app_name\" content=\"LinkedIn\">\n\n<!---->\n          <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/al2o9zrvru7aqj8e1x2rzsrca\">\n\n        <script>\n          function getDfd() {let yFn,nFn;const p=new Promise(function(y, n){yFn=y;nFn=n;});p.resolve=yFn;p.reject=nFn;return p;}\n          window.lazyloader = getDfd();\n          window.tracking = getDfd();\n          window.impressionTracking = getDfd();\n          window.ingraphTracking = getDfd();\n          window.appDetection = getDfd();\n          window.pemTracking = getDfd();\n          window.appRedirectCompleted = getDfd();\n        </script>\n\n<!---->\n        \n        \n    \n\n    \n    \n    \n\n    \n\n    \n    \n    \n\n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n\n    \n\n        \n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Interview Experience – Amazon | SDE-2 (Senior Backend Engineer) 🧠💻\nRecently completed the interview process at Amazon for an SDE-2 role.\n It was intense, well-structured, and heavily focused on problem-solving, ownership, and depth.\n\nSharing a quick breakdown — hope this helps fellow backend engineers 🚀\n🟢 Online Assessment (OA)\nCoding Challenge (90 mins): 2 DSA problems, strong focus on edge cases, optimal solutions, and clean code\nWork Simulation (15 mins): Real-world SDE decisions, prioritization, and trade-offs\nWork Style Surveys (10 mins): Ownership, collaboration, and handling ambiguity\n🟢 Coding Round\nQ1: Longest Bitonic Subarray\n (Expected both brute force + optimal approach with time/space analysis)\nQ2: Modify a tree so all node values lie within a given range\n (Traversal strategy, recursion, edge cases)\n🟢 LLD Round\nDesigned a multi-turn chat system with LLM\nSession management &amp; conversation history\nContext handling for multi-turn chats\nAPIs, caching, and cost optimization\n Strong focus on design clarity and trade-offs\n🟢 HLD Round\nDesigned a NoSQL database system\nDiscussed APIs, functional &amp; non-functional requirements\nCapacity constraints, data modeling, read/write patterns\n🟢 Bar Raiser Round\nDeep dive into my projects (HLD, decisions, impact, scalability)\nFollowed by a DSA question\n Lots of “why?” — checking ownership and leadership mindset\n\nNo matter the outcome, it was a great learning experience.\n On to the next one 🚀\nIf you’re preparing for backend/SDE-2 interviews, happy to help or discuss 🙂\n\n#InterviewExperience #Amazon #BackendEngineering\n #DSA #LLD #SystemDesign #Java #SDELife\">\n  <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Interview Experience – Amazon | SDE-2 (Senior Backend Engineer) 🧠💻\nRecently completed the interview process at Amazon for an SDE-2 role.\n It was intense, well-structured, and heavily focused on problem-solving, ownership, and depth.\n\nSharing a quick breakdown — hope this helps fellow backend engineers 🚀\n🟢 Online Assessment (OA)\nCoding Challenge (90 mins): 2 DSA problems, strong focus on edge cases, optimal solutions, and clean code\nWork Simulation (15 mins): Real-world SDE decisions, prioritization, and trade-offs\nWork Style Surveys (10 mins): Ownership, collaboration, and handling ambiguity\n🟢 Coding Round\nQ1: Longest Bitonic Subarray\n (Expected both brute force + optimal approach with time/space analysis)\nQ2: Modify a tree so all node values lie within a given range\n (Traversal strategy, recursion, edge cases)\n🟢 LLD Round\nDesigned a multi-turn chat system with LLM\nSession management &amp; conversation history\nContext handling for multi-turn chats\nAPIs, caching, and cost optimization\n Strong focus on design clarity and trade-offs\n🟢 HLD Round\nDesigned a NoSQL database system\nDiscussed APIs, functional &amp; non-functional requirements\nCapacity constraints, data modeling, read/write patterns\n🟢 Bar Raiser Round\nDeep dive into my projects (HLD, decisions, impact, scalability)\nFollowed by a DSA question\n Lots of “why?” — checking ownership and leadership mindset\n\nNo matter the outcome, it was a great learning experience.\n On to the next one 🚀\nIf you’re preparing for backend/SDE-2 interviews, happy to help or discuss 🙂\n\n#InterviewExperience #Amazon #BackendEngineering\n #DSA #LLD #SystemDesign #Java #SDELife\">\n  <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Interview Experience – Amazon | SDE-2 (Senior Backend Engineer) 🧠💻\nRecently completed the interview process at Amazon for an SDE-2 role.\n It was intense, well-structured, and heavily focused on problem-solving, ownership, and depth.\n\nSharing a quick breakdown — hope this helps fellow backend engineers 🚀\n🟢 Online Assessment (OA)\nCoding Challenge (90 mins): 2 DSA problems, strong focus on edge cases, optimal solutions, and clean code\nWork Simulation (15 mins): Real-world SDE decisions, prioritization, and trade-offs\nWork Style Surveys (10 mins): Ownership, collaboration, and handling ambiguity\n🟢 Coding Round\nQ1: Longest Bitonic Subarray\n (Expected both brute force + optimal approach with time/space analysis)\nQ2: Modify a tree so all node values lie within a given range\n (Traversal strategy, recursion, edge cases)\n🟢 LLD Round\nDesigned a multi-turn chat system with LLM\nSession management &amp; conversation history\nContext handling for multi-turn chats\nAPIs, caching, and cost optimization\n Strong focus on design clarity and trade-offs\n🟢 HLD Round\nDesigned a NoSQL database system\nDiscussed APIs, functional &amp; non-functional requirements\nCapacity constraints, data modeling, read/write patterns\n🟢 Bar Raiser Round\nDeep dive into my projects (HLD, decisions, impact, scalability)\nFollowed by a DSA question\n Lots of “why?” — checking ownership and leadership mindset\n\nNo matter the outcome, it was a great learning experience.\n On to the next one 🚀\nIf you’re preparing for backend/SDE-2 interviews, happy to help or discuss 🙂\n\n#InterviewExperience #Amazon #BackendEngineering\n #DSA #LLD #SystemDesign #Java #SDELife\">\n\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"#interviewexperience #amazon #backendengineering #dsa #lld #systemdesign #java #sdelife | Ravi Kumar\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"#interviewexperience #amazon #backendengineering #dsa #lld #systemdesign #java #sdelife | Ravi Kumar\">\n    <title>#interviewexperience #amazon #backendengineering #dsa #lld #systemdesign #java #sdelife | Ravi Kumar</title>\n\n      <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n\n    <meta property=\"lnkd:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7419793472636866560\">\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\">\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ravikumar9199_interviewexperience-amazon-backendengineering-activity-7419793472636866560-qZ7e\">\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"LinkedIn\">\n      <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\">\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/c45fy346jw096z9pbphyyhdz7\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/c45fy346jw096z9pbphyyhdz7\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@linkedin\">\n    <meta property=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ravikumar9199_interviewexperience-amazon-backendengineering-activity-7419793472636866560-qZ7e\">\n<!---->      <meta name=\"clientSideIngraphs\" content=\"1\" data-gauge-metric-endpoint=\"/feedcontent-guest/api/ingraphs/gauge\" data-counter-metric-endpoint=\"/feedcontent-guest/api/ingraphs/counter\">\n  \n\n        <link rel=\"